A||||3||JohnnyK||3.1 Liter Upgrade?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||03-11-2000||02:28 PM||||Well, I bought this Fiero, and the 4cyl engine is kaput (and I won't be happy with 92 horsepower anyways)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So I was wondering if I could just throw in a 1990 3.1 Liter engine from a Corsica or something (or any year later than that?) Are the engine mounts and such the same as the 2.5 4cyl? (It is an '85 5spd).. Will the tranny hook up? Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||03-11-2000||08:47 PM||||    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  Swaping engines is not quite that easy.  Nothing lines up usually.  Engines from different cars usually don't quite match. Any old transmission doesn't exactly bolt on to any old engine.<P>When my 2.8 was gone, the mechanic said he'd get me another, He found a 2.8 from a Camaro.. it wasn't right, no way to fit.  <P>Call up Dan Campbell, Pisa Corp. He sent me a remanufactured 3.1.<P>Call up Joe Wynman..Quad 4 conversion.<P>Call up the Fiero Shop in Weston, Ontario 416 747 5728 or web site <A HREF="http://web.idirect.com/~sabex" TARGET=_blank>http://web.idirect.com/~sabex</A> <P>They do engine swaps.<P>Or find another Iron Duke 92 hp and do the easy switch.  If you got enough $$, you can do anything.<P>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 03-11-2000).]<P>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 03-11-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 03-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||03-12-2000||04:43 PM||||If you want easier installation and lower cost, you could always find a 2.8 from another Fiero, but even then there's stuff that needs to be changed.||||reg||1
Z||000003||kupop87gt||03-12-2000||05:15 PM||||The 3.1 is just a 2.8 with a longer stroke. It would be the easiest swap around, besides a 2.8 I assume. A RWD 60 degree V6 is probably a different story. Except for an easy 3.4 swap; you must use a RWD version.||||reg||1
